# Secrets — never commit.
#
# Deny every .env* and then allow back the two examples, rather than listing
# the ones to ignore. The old list named `.env`, `.env.local` and
# `.env.*.local` — which did not cover `.env.prod`, the file
# `.env.prod.example` tells you to create and fill with a database password.
# A deny-list of secret files is only ever one filename away from leaking one.
.env*
!.env.example
!.env.prod.example

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# Node
node_modules/
dist/
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Editors / OS
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
